  m_Name: 5_SurvivalOutsideHost
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: 'Survival Outside Host:'
  Description: "In vitro experiments suggest that RVF virus can persist for a few
    days in some protein-rich environments such as tissues. In a neutral or alkaline
    pH, mixed with serum or other proteins, the virus may survive for as long as 4
    months at 4\xB0C (40\xB0F) and 8 years below 0\xB0C (32\xB0F). It is quickly destroyed
    by pH changes in decomposing carcasses. "
